ns un arbre détaché, échoue sur un test lu, chaque commande de tâche passe sur la tête de la branche,\nPreflight est verte à la révision citée, la relecture s'arrête à deux tours, la branche arrive sur\n`main` en un commit, le dossier est exporté au versement.\n\nCe qui manque encore : la mutation sur les lignes introduites pour une cible Node, que les\nrelecteurs font à la main, et le worker Pi confiné de 495 à la place des sessions Claude Code.\n6297959 docs: the registry records the file added under node_modules as fixed\ne581532 refactor: the installed-dependency path test is written once and read by both the size limit and the protected-path rule\n099a3c0 test: a file added under tests/ by a candidate on a vitest target stays an allowed new test\na3ecb9e fix: a file added under node_modules is refused as a protected path while a file added under tests is still allowed as a new test\nc97cd63 docs: the story e05s01 promises that a file added under node_modules is refused as a protected path\n561d36d test: a candidate that adds a file under node_modules that can shadow a package the vitest control loads is refused as a protected path\ne47bc10 docs: the registry records that a file added under node_modules is not refused though it can shadow a dependency the vitest control loads\n8ef748d fix: the cache vitest writes under node_modules/.vite and .vite-temp is neither copied nor observed, so running the suite in the copy does not modify a protected path\n0ae0ce1 test: the cache vitest writes under node_modules/.vite and .vite-temp is not in the candidate manifest while a change to an installed dependency still is\n4b1a753 docs: the story e05s01 promises that the cache vitest writes under node_modules is not a change to an installed dependency\n1bf26b6 docs: the registry records that the Seatbelt test of the generic runner grants the temporary directory and so cannot fail under it\nc5b7c34 test: the verification sandbox lets the vitest control create the directory where Vite compiles its configuration\nc16cd97 test: the report directory the vitest control declares writable is what lets the verification sandbox create it, even when the test tree lives under the temporary directory\ncec91d9 docs: the scripts.test forms comment says why only a directly started runner is read\n43ed18d refactor: the vitest control tests build a real candidate manifest and share the derived control instead of casting and repeating it\n8775ba7 chore: the story branch carries the cycle fix that finishes a red-green pass resumed after its work was done\na096d21 chore: the story branch carries the cycle fix that replays only the test-only commits of a red-green pass\n89fb463 feat: the vitest unit control protects the installed dependencies so a candidate that modifies the vitest that judges it is refused\n8846bb9 test: a candidate that modifies node_modules/vitest/dist/index.js is refused as a protected path of the vitest unit control\n2f7ec65 fix: the observation digests an installed dependency whatever its size while a file elsewhere is still bounded by the per-file limit\n67b2cb8 test: a file under node_modules above the size limit is observed with its digest while the same file elsewhere is still noted as exceeding it\n388131e fix: the vitest unit control declares the target directory writable so the sandbox lets vitest create its report directory\nd6ccf80 test: the vitest unit control writes its report under the verification sandbox even when the copy carries no target directory\nc61a442 docs: the story e05s01 promises that the vitest report is written where the sandbox lets it be created and that the installed dependencies are observed and protected\n3760b20 docs: the registry records that a refused scripts.test leaves the protocol frozen on the lint control alone\ne64827a fix: a scripts.test that is not a string is read as absent instead of crashing the Node stack detection\n491a0dd test: a scripts.test that is not a string is read as absent by the